meta {
  name: Get Session
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/portal/session
  body: none
  auth: none
}

script:post-response {
  const token = res.body?.data?.csrfToken;
  if (token) bru.setVar("portalCsrfToken", token);
}

docs {
  Requires the server to run with `ENABLE_SELF_SERVE=true` ("Mis citas" is off by default: every
  /portal path answers 404) and a `portal_session` cookie. No login issues that cookie now that the
  codes are gone, so this request only works against a session minted for a future login.

  Needs the `portal_session` cookie. Returns
  `{ contact, contactChannel, expiresAt, csrfToken, providerSlug, consentRequired, bookingOpen }` with the
  same keys and types whether or not the contact belongs to a patient. `contact` is what the session
  proved, an email or a number, on `contactChannel`. `consentRequired` is false only for an existing
  patient who accepted the current privacy policy version. `bookingOpen` is false while the provider
  has paused booking or setup is incomplete: the session still works (see and cancel appointments),
  but booking and rescheduling answer 404. Any session problem (missing, expired, tampered, provider
  deleted/inactive/without a slug, portal off) answers 401 "Invalid session".
}
